IMPORT `tn67-nouns`

-- Row il-67. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: four items (I1, I2, I3, I4), the nine sections they name (statuses as the instruments read give them), and the control beside I4 (the citation in section 53).
-- Tests of the controls are in tn67-tests-controls.l4, tests that pin the readings are in tn67-tests-readings.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose (four, one per item) are in tn67-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[shNNN-pPPP]` lines quote the Hebrew read from the deposited page image of Sefer HaChukim (SH) issue NNN, printed page PPP (registers/source-bundle/pages/). They are official instruments.
-- The Hebrew on those lines was copied from the row's reading of the image and checked against the deposited crop; the text layers of these old pages are partly wrong (NOTES.md says which lines were compared with a text layer and which were not).
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.

§ `References`

